      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the number $125$ is a perfect cube.\n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{-125},$ we express $-125$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-125} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-5)\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (-5)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-5)^{3}} & = \\\\ -5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
